{% doc %}
  Shop by age — the first thing the curtain brings up over the film.

  The homepage opens on the film hero, which §08b of sv-system.css pins;
  this section is the page that arrives over it, and the first question
  it answers is the first question every parent shopping for a child
  has: how old? Four ages, four circles, and under each circle the size
  runs it splits into — a visitor lands on the exact shelf in two taps
  without ever reading a menu.

  ── Shape ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  cat    one block per age band: a circular photograph, the name, the
         range, then the subdivision chips. Circles rather than cards:
         the mock the owner supplied uses them, they read as portraits
         rather than products, and they cannot be mistaken for the
         product grid that follows one page deeper.
  subs   up to five label+link pairs per band, each its own setting —
         explicit pairs rather than a parsed textarea, so Admin can
         retarget one chip without re-typing the rest, and a blank pair
         simply doesn't render.

  ── Rules kept ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Tokens only; type comes from sv-system.css primitives. Motion per
  §08 — transform and opacity, IntersectionObserver, no scroll
  listeners; armed by sv-motion-gate as the FIRST child so nothing is
  painted visible and then pulled to opacity 0, and with script off the
  section is a complete static document. Links come from Admin settings,
  never typed here.
{% enddoc %}

{%- comment -%}
  The id is an anchor, not decoration: the hero's "Shop by age" card
  links to #shop-by-age so the card lands on this band rather than
  tipping the visitor into All products, which answers none of the
  question the card asks.
{%- endcomment -%}
<section id="shop-by-age" class="sv-age sv-amb-host" data-sv>

  {%- render 'sv-motion-gate' -%}

  {%- comment -%}
    Ambient ground — promoted to the system (§08c + snippets/sv-ambient)
    once the owner asked for it to run through the page. The host class
    on the root and the .w column carry the layering contract.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- render 'sv-ambient' -%}

  <div class="w w--wide">

    <header class="sv-age__head">
      {%- if section.settings.eyebrow != blank -%}
        <p class="eyebrow sv-age__eyebrow" data-sv-motion>{{ section.settings.eyebrow }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        The heading is optional — the owner runs this strip on the
        eyebrow alone. The document keeps its h2 either way: a landmark
        a sighted visitor doesn't need is still the one a screen-reader
        user navigates by.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if section.settings.title != blank -%}
        <h2 class="sv-age__title" data-sv-motion>{{ section.settings.title }}</h2>
      {%- else -%}
        <h2 class="sv-visually-hidden">{{ section.settings.eyebrow | default: 'Shop by age' }}</h2>
      {%- endif -%}
    </header>

    <div class="sv-age__grid">
      {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
        {%- liquid
          assign cat_url = block.settings.link
          if cat_url == blank
            assign cat_url = routes.all_products_collection_url
          endif
        -%}
        <div class="sv-age__cat" data-sv-motion style="--i: {{ forloop.index0 }}" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>

          <a class="sv-age__disc" href="{{ cat_url }}" style="--sv-fy: {{ block.settings.focus | default: 20 }}%" aria-label="{{ block.settings.title | escape }}{% if block.settings.range != blank %}, {{ block.settings.range | escape }}{% endif %}">
            {%- if block.settings.image -%}
              <img
                src="{{ block.settings.image | image_url: width: 480 }}"
                srcset="{{ block.settings.image | image_url: width: 300 }} 300w, {{ block.settings.image | image_url: width: 480 }} 480w, {{ block.settings.image | image_url: width: 720 }} 720w"
                sizes="(max-width: 760px) 40vw, 240px"
                alt="{{ block.settings.image.alt | default: block.settings.title | escape }}"
                width="{{ block.settings.image.width }}"
                height="{{ block.settings.image.height }}"
                loading="lazy"
              >
            {%- else -%}
              {%- comment -%} §06's placeholder field, in the round. {%- endcomment -%}
              <span class="im sv-age__ph" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            {%- endif -%}
          </a>

          <h3 class="sv-age__name"><a href="{{ cat_url }}">{{ block.settings.title }}</a></h3>

          {%- if block.settings.range != blank -%}
            <p class="lab lab--grey sv-age__range">{{ block.settings.range }}</p>
          {%- endif -%}

          {%- capture subs -%}
            {%- for i in (1..5) -%}
              {%- assign lkey = 'sub_' | append: i | append: '_label' -%}
              {%- assign ukey = 'sub_' | append: i | append: '_url' -%}
              {%- assign slabel = block.settings[lkey] -%}
              {%- if slabel != blank -%}
                {%- assign surl = block.settings[ukey] | default: cat_url -%}
                <li>
                  <a class="sv-age__sub" href="{{ surl }}" aria-label="{{ block.settings.title | escape }}, {{ slabel | escape }}">{{ slabel }}</a>
                </li>
              {%- endif -%}
            {%- endfor -%}
          {%- endcapture -%}
          {%- if subs != blank -%}
            <ul class="sv-age__subs">{{ subs }}</ul>
          {%- endif -%}

        </div>
      {%- endfor -%}
    </div>

  </div>

  {%- comment -%}
    Motion driver — sv-about's, verbatim in shape. Reveals once and
    unobserves; the hidden state exists only under `.sv-motion-ready`,
    which the gate at the top adds, so a failed script leaves the
    section fully readable.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <script>
    (() => {
      const root = document.currentScript.closest('.sv-age');
      if (!root) return;
      const targets = root.querySelectorAll('[data-sv-motion]');
      if (!('IntersectionObserver' in window) ||
          matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches) {
        targets.forEach(el => el.classList.add('sv-vis'));
        return;
      }
      const io = new IntersectionObserver(entries => {
        entries.forEach(e => {
          if (!e.isIntersecting) return;
          e.target.classList.add('sv-vis');
          io.unobserve(e.target);
        });
      }, { threshold: 0.12, rootMargin: '0px 0px -6% 0px' });
      targets.forEach(el => io.observe(el));

      /* Fail-safe. A tab loaded in the background defers observer
         callbacks; anything already on screen shortly after load is
         shown outright, the observer still governs the rest. */
      setTimeout(() => {
        targets.forEach(el => {
          const r = el.getBoundingClientRect();
          if (r.top < innerHeight && r.bottom > 0) el.classList.add('sv-vis');
        });
      }, 1200);
    })();
  </script>
</section>

{% stylesheet %}
  /* Tokens only. Specificity note: the §02 reset is (0,1,1), so every
     rule that must beat it is written .sv-age .sv-age__* at (0,2,0). */

  /* The ambient ground and its layering contract live in sv-system.css
     §08c (.sv-amb-host on the root, .w lifted above the layer). */

  /* Compact by request: the default section breath (--g, 160px) read as
     dead ivory at full width, and the band below sits close so the two
     read as one page. Double class outranks §02's section[data-sv] at
     (0,1,1). */
  [data-sv].sv-age {
    padding: var(--d) 0 var(--b);
  }

  .sv-age .sv-age__head {
    text-align: center;
    margin-bottom: var(--c);
  }
  .sv-age .sv-age__title {
    margin-top: var(--a);
  }
  /* The base .eyebrow is .66rem warm grey — sized for a corner label,
     not a centred line introducing a section. Stepped up to read. */
  .sv-age .sv-age__eyebrow {
    justify-content: center;
    margin-bottom: 0;
    font-size: .92rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: .26em;
    color: var(--emerald);
  }
  /* .eyebrow's gold dash sits before the text; centred it needs a twin
     after, or the line reads pushed left. */
  .sv-age .sv-age__eyebrow::after {
    content: "";
    width: 44px;
    height: 1px;
    background: var(--tan);
  }

  .sv-age .sv-age__grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
    gap: var(--c);
  }

  .sv-age .sv-age__cat {
    text-align: center;
  }

  .sv-age .sv-age__disc {
    display: block;
    width: min(100%, 240px);
    margin: 0 auto;
    aspect-ratio: 1;
    border-radius: 50%;
    overflow: hidden;
    position: relative;
    box-shadow: var(--sh-s);
    background: linear-gradient(150deg, #F5F0E2, #E9E1CD 55%, #DCD2B8);
    transition: transform var(--std) var(--e), box-shadow var(--std) var(--e);
  }
  .sv-age .sv-age__disc:hover {
    transform: translateY(-4px);
    box-shadow: var(--sh);
  }
  .sv-age .sv-age__disc img {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
    /* Portraits carry the face in their upper third; a centred crop takes
       the top of the head off. The crop window anchors near the top of
       the photograph instead, per-band tunable from Admin. */
    object-position: 50% var(--sv-fy, 20%);
    transition: transform var(--slow) var(--e);
  }
  .sv-age .sv-age__disc:hover img {
    transform: scale(1.05);
  }
  .sv-age .sv-age__ph {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    border-radius: 50%;
  }

  .sv-age .sv-age__name {
    margin-top: var(--a);
    font-size: clamp(1.25rem, 1.8vw, 1.5rem);
  }
  .sv-age .sv-age__name a {
    color: var(--ink);
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .sv-age .sv-age__name a:hover {
    color: var(--emerald);
  }

  /* .lab--grey is a corner label; as a line under a name it needs ink
     and a step up to read. */
  .sv-age .sv-age__range {
    margin-top: 8px;
    font-size: .74rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: .22em;
    color: var(--ink);
    opacity: .75;
  }

  .sv-age .sv-age__subs {
    margin-top: var(--a);
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 8px;
  }
  .sv-age .sv-age__sub {
    display: inline-block;
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: .66rem;
    font-weight: 400;
    letter-spacing: .14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink);
    text-decoration: none;
    padding: 7px 14px;
    border: 1px solid rgba(198, 161, 91, .45);
    border-radius: 999px;
    transition: background-color var(--micro) var(--e),
                color var(--micro) var(--e),
                border-color var(--micro) var(--e);
  }
  .sv-age .sv-age__sub:hover {
    background: var(--emerald);
    border-color: var(--emerald);
    color: var(--cream);
  }

  @media (max-width: 980px) {
    .sv-age .sv-age__grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
      gap: var(--d) var(--b);
    }
  }

  /* Motion — armed by the gate, released by the driver. The circles
     arrive as a run, each a beat after the last, per §08's stagger. */
  .sv-age.sv-motion-ready [data-sv-motion] {
    opacity: 0;
    transform: translateY(var(--rise));
    transition: opacity .85s var(--entrance), transform .85s var(--entrance);
    transition-delay: calc(var(--i, 0) * var(--stagger));
  }
  .sv-age.sv-motion-ready [data-sv-motion].sv-vis {
    opacity: 1;
    transform: none;
  }
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "SV Shop by Age",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "sv-age-mount",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "text", "id": "eyebrow", "label": "Eyebrow", "default": "Start with the age" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "title", "label": "Heading", "info": "Leave blank to run the strip on the eyebrow alone (a hidden heading keeps the page's structure for screen readers).", "default": "Shop by age" }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "category",
      "name": "Age band",
      "settings": [
        { "type": "image_picker", "id": "image", "label": "Photograph", "info": "Square crop; shown in a circle." },
        {
          "type": "range",
          "id": "focus",
          "label": "Portrait focus",
          "info": "Where the circle's crop window sits on the photo: 0 is the very top, 100 the bottom.",
          "min": 0,
          "max": 100,
          "step": 5,
          "unit": "%",
          "default": 20
        },
        { "type": "text", "id": "title", "label": "Name", "default": "Newborn" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "range", "label": "Range", "default": "0–12 months" },
        { "type": "url", "id": "link", "label": "Link" },
        { "type": "header", "content": "Subdivisions" },
        { "type": "paragraph", "content": "Up to five. A blank label drops the pair; a blank link falls back to the band's own link." },
        { "type": "text", "id": "sub_1_label", "label": "Chip 1 · label" },
        { "type": "url", "id": "sub_1_url", "label": "Chip 1 · link" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "sub_2_label", "label": "Chip 2 · label" },
        { "type": "url", "id": "sub_2_url", "label": "Chip 2 · link" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "sub_3_label", "label": "Chip 3 · label" },
        { "type": "url", "id": "sub_3_url", "label": "Chip 3 · link" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "sub_4_label", "label": "Chip 4 · label" },
        { "type": "url", "id": "sub_4_url", "label": "Chip 4 · link" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "sub_5_label", "label": "Chip 5 · label" },
        { "type": "url", "id": "sub_5_url", "label": "Chip 5 · link" }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "max_blocks": 6,
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "SV Shop by Age",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "category",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Newborn",
            "range": "0–12 months",
            "sub_1_label": "0–3 m",
            "sub_2_label": "3–6 m",
            "sub_3_label": "6–9 m",
            "sub_4_label": "9–12 m"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "category",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Toddler",
            "range": "1–3 years",
            "sub_1_label": "12–18 m",
            "sub_2_label": "18–24 m",
            "sub_3_label": "2–3 y"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "category",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Kids",
            "range": "3–6 years",
            "sub_1_label": "3–4 y",
            "sub_2_label": "4–5 y",
            "sub_3_label": "5–6 y"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "category",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Big kids",
            "range": "6–8 years",
            "sub_1_label": "6–7 y",
            "sub_2_label": "7–8 y"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
